Thread affinity on OHOS, in llama.cpp's ggml.

Same two-line fix as qwentts-ggml-ohos-affinity.patch, against a different
checkout of the same file -- read that one for why. The paths differ because
here ggml is a subdirectory of the repo rather than a submodule, so this
applies in the llama.cpp work tree, not one level down.

This was found already applied in the checkout, by hand, undocumented. It is
recorded here so an update does not quietly drop it.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
index 87a329f..f472393 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#define _GNU_SOURCE 1 // OHOS: cpu_set_t/CPU_ZERO live behind this guard in musl sched.h
 #define _CRT_SECURE_NO_DEPRECATE // Disables "unsafe" warnings on Windows
 #define _USE_MATH_DEFINES // For M_PI on MSVC
 
@@ -2650,7 +2651,7 @@ static bool ggml_thread_apply_affinity(const bool * mask) {
         }
     }
 
-#ifdef __ANDROID__
+#if defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(__OHOS__) // OHOS has sched_setaffinity but no pthread_setaffinity_np
     err = sched_setaffinity(0, sizeof(cpuset), &cpuset);
     if (err < 0) {
         err = errno;
